# Copy to signal-github/.env and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Why a file and not `export GITHUB_TOKEN=...`: shell environment variables do
# not survive between agent tool calls on Windows, so a token set in one call is
# gone by the next. src/gh.py loads this file at import and never overrides a
# variable already present in the real environment.
#
# The token needs NO scopes for public data. Generate at
# https://github.com/settings/tokens  ->  "Generate new token (classic)"  ->
# tick nothing at all  ->  copy the value below.
#
# What it buys, measured from response headers (reports/step0.md):
#   core REST    60/hour  ->  5,000/hour   (83x)
#   code search  401      ->  30/minute    (unblocks a whole retrieval axis)
#
# Note: as of 2026-08-03 the `archive` transport in gh.py fetches a repo's whole
# file tree AND contents from codeload with no core spend at all, so depth no
# longer depends on this token. The token is still what unblocks code search.

GITHUB_TOKEN=
